details:
(a) whether the National Green Tribunal has set up any committee to inspect the site and probe the extent, if any, of illegal mining in the Delh-NCR region;
(b) if so, the timeline by when the committee is expected to present its report;
(c) whether the concerned committee has been directed to inspect the entire area and needs to evaluate the possibility of night time illegal mining; and
(d) when the physical inspection by the committee was last conducted?

(a) how many Jan Aushadhi Kendras are functional throughout the country;
(b) the details thereof, State-wise;
(c) whether Government has outlined any plan to expand this network of Jan Aushadhi Kendras; and
(d) whether Government is setting any target for opening of more Kendras?

(a) whether Government is aware of the fact that the failure of signals on Railway tracks is suspected to be the reason of many fatal accidents or derailment in the last three years;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether the Ministry has ordered an audit of the signalling systems across its network to rectify the deficiencies and to ensure safe train operations; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) how many cases of EPFO has been settled during 2024-25 and 2025-26;
(b) whether it is a fact that there is no need to upload the cheque leaf image to file the claims; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Virupaksha Temple’s (Hampi, Karnataka) pavilion has collapsed; 
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether ASI has begun dismantling the entire pavilion of the Temple?

(a) whether there is any data on the drop-out rate for boys and girls in schools;
(b) if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to reduce the drop-out rates in schools, the details thereof?

(a) the details of gaps in the Right to Education that need to be addressed;
(b) whether Private schools have mandatorily reserve 25 per cent seats for admission of students in the Economically Weaker Sections (EWS) category;
(c) whether Right to Education directs that a students should be given free education till the age of fourteen years; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether there is any reduction observed in Maternal Mortality Rate;
(b) if so, the percentage of reduction recorded in the year 2021-24;
(c) whether there is any reduction in the under-five mortality rate recorded in the year 2021-24; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether it is permissible to repair and renovate existing buildings and structures within the prohibited area of 100 meters as per ASI regulations;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether any permission is required to be obtained from National Monument Authority for such repair and renovation work in prohibited areas?

(a) whether it is a fact that rules in regard to construction, repairs or renovations of protected monuments and prohibited areas by ASI have recently been changed;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) since when the above amendment have come into force?

(a) the details of funds allocated for the security of heritage sites during the last three years;
(b) whether there is any plan to review the security of those sites, in view of recent acts of vandalism by tourists at such sites; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of Konkan Geoglyphy carvings which have been documented so far and the number of locations where they appear; 
(b) whether there is any threat to Konkan Geoglyphs by urban development projects and illegal mining; and
(c) if so, the details thereof and the plans proposed to avert the threat?

(a) whether there is any performance Index being framed to assess the school education quality;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether there is any data on the issue of absenteeism of students in schools; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?
